+$id: http://devicetree.org/schemas/clock/allwinner,sun60i-a733-cpu-ccu.yaml#
+$schema: http://devicetree.org/meta-schemas/core.yaml#
+
+title: Allwinner A733 CPU PLL Clock Control Unit
+
+maintainers:
+  - DockSeed <dockseed@proton.me>
+
+description: >
+  The A733 (sun60iw2) keeps the CPU clocks out of the main CCU, in a block of
+  its own at 0x08870000 that the manual calls CPU_PLL_CFG. It holds four PLLs
+  (CPU_BACK, CPU_L for cores 0-5, CPU_B for cores 6-7 and CPU_DSU for the
+  DynamIQ cluster) and one glitch-free clock mux per cluster.
+
+  The block has no resets and no bus gates, so it exposes clocks only.
+
+  The mapping must cover CPU_SLOW_CLK_SEL_REG at offset 0x3034, which selects
+  what the muxes' bypass input actually is; a size of 0x3038 is the minimum.
